     A****************************************************************
     A** NOTE: Though PBILLS no longer hard deletes EOMBs, 'M' type
     A**       EOMBs(Case Management T/Ms) will be hard deleted if
     A**       EOMB is uninvoiced and there are no T/M activity
     A**       line items.  This happens if 1)An 'M' type EOMB is
     A**       created but no T/M activity added. or 2)An 'M' type
     A**       EOMB had T/M activity, but then all activity is deleted.
     A**       This will result in breaks in the sequence of EOMB#s.
